==Enemy==
One Celeboodle has the power to destroy your cats easily, but fortunately, she is a single-target attacker, so spamming meatshields can easily stall her. This enemy is usually spawned in groups, but they rarely last long enough to cause much damage.

Celeboodle has a high money drop for how easy she is to kill and how frequently she tends to be spawned, giving almost 3,000¢ with the [[Super Register]] and Accounting upgrade maxed.

==Strategy==
Though she deals a lot of damage and has a moderate attack rate, Celeboodle is not an Area Attack enemy. She has rather low health and is considered a glass cannon. The best strategy is to spam [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshield-class cats]] ([[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Tank Cat]], etc.) to protect any powerful cats, such as [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] or any other long-ranged [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attacker]]. Again, one strike from a Bahamut Cat can usually put a stop to these these pesky poodles, while giving a fair amount of money back.

In mid-game, this enemy becomes as threatening as a giant money bag. Even large groups (such as the ones present in [[Sweet XP (Insane)]]) can be controlled by Area Attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] or [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed UFO Cat]]. You can even use [[:Category:Cats with Money Up ability|Cats with Money Up abilities]] like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] or [[Talents|Talented]] [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] to exploit their somewhat high money drop.

In [[Uncanny Legends]], Celeboodle becomes more threatening again, due to the intense buffs boosting her already high damage and the fact that she is combined with stronger enemies. She might not have the most health, but she will be able to tank hits from high-damaging units such as [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Teacher BearCat]], Can Can Cat, Bullet Train Cat and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]]. Additionally, she will kill [[:Category:Tanker-class Cats|tankers]] very quickly, so the use of smaller meatshields are recommended instead. If you are using [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|rushers]], like Awakened Bahamut Cat, make sure there are enough meatshields to stall Celeboodle before sending them out so they can get a quick kill.

